#!/bin/bash
# Keep uv current on `omarchy update`.
#
# uv comes from astral's install script (run by `omarchy-install-dev-env python`), which
# drops it in ~/.local/bin outside both pacman and mise. That means nothing in omarchy's
# update path touches it: omarchy-update refreshes system packages, AUR packages and mise
# tools, and uv is none of the three, so it would sit at whatever version first landed.
# `uv self update` is the supported way to move that kind of install forward.
#
# This is the one thing we lost by moving uv off pacman, where `omarchy update`'s system
# package step kept it fresh for free. The hook buys it back using omarchy's own
# extension point rather than by keeping a second uv around.
#
# omarchy-hook treats a non-zero exit as non-fatal (it prints "Hook failed" and carries
# on), so nothing here can break an update. The guard is for machines that never ran the
# python dev-env, and pacman-installed uv refuses `self update` on its own anyway.
command -v uv >/dev/null || exit 0
uv self update
